On Tuesday, October 1, 2013 4:08:57 AM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> I just wrote a section on why naming is important for
> the Stan 2.0 manual :-)  But like doc, they can be
> misleading.  (Like the user who was using "prec" for
> a covariance matrix.)

Another thing that is confusing at the moment, is that if someone wants to use a parameterized precision matrix, they have to declare it as a cov_matrix:

parameters {
  cov_matrix[K] Sigma_inv;
}
model {
  ...
  y ~ multi_normal_prec(mu, Sigma_inv);
  ...
}

Ben

