On 10/1/13 8:30 AM, Ben Goodrich wrote:
> Another thing that is confusing at the moment, is that if someone wants to use a parameterized precision matrix, they
> have to declare it as a cov_matrix:
>
> |
> parameters {
>    cov_matrix[K] Sigma_inv;
> }
> model {
>    ...
>    y ~ multi_normal_prec(mu, Sigma_inv);
>    ...
> }
> |

That was indeed a bad choice on my part for the variable
type.  And it looks like I may have made the same bad decision
for the cholesky_cov we're about to introduce.

Do you think we should change it to positive_definite_symmetric
and deprecate the use of cov_matrix?

- Bob

