I would suggest spd_matrix as the type name since the full thing seems painful.  (Also, linguistically symmetric usually comes first.  Not sure there's a good reason, I've just never really seen "positive definite symmetric" before.)

Perhaps cov_matrix (and maybe an added prec_matrix?) could be added as aliases to reduce confusion for users?

Cheers,
Marcus

