Here's what the R extensions manual says:

   The mandatory ï¿½Versionï¿½ field gives the version of the package. This is a
   sequence of at least two (and usually three) non-negative integers separated
   by single ï¿½.ï¿½ or ï¿½-ï¿½ characters. The canonical form is as shown in the example,
   and a version such as ï¿½0.01ï¿½ or ï¿½0.01.0ï¿½ will be handled as if it were ï¿½0.1-0ï¿½.
   It is not a decimal number, so for example 0.9 < 0.75 since 9 < 75.

So I'd suggest

    2.0.0-1

because it won't conflict with Stan 2.0.1 and won't require the versions to
go backward when you release an official 2.0.0.

- Bob

