Hi,

Python has some rules about versioning
(http://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0386/) and I'm not sure '-' is valid.
I think it may conflict with Debian packaging versioning. At this point perhaps
a fourth number is the best bet for Python at least, e.g., 2.0.0.1?

I'll try to get PyStan up to date (it's about a month behind) in time for the
final release. It's certainly beta -- I've been using it in my work for the past
two months without any problems. It compiles cleanly on Linux and OS X.

Best, -a

