On the subject of autodiff, has anyone looked at how Theano
(http://deeplearning.net/software/theano/) is doing symbolic
differentiation? Might be a blind alley, but it seems like it'd solve
some problems if Stan could do symbolic rather than automatic
differentiation. (Lower runtime memory use, more compiler
optimizations, and less complicated higher-order differentiation come
to mind as potential advantages.) And the deep neural network models
Theano's trying to optimize are not fundamentally different than the
models Stan's trying to sample from—both just need gradients of a
scalar cost or log-likelihood.

Matt

