Subject: inv_wishart behavior
Message-ID: <vqB52U_MNFA.91uDkgmR9Q0J@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/vqB52U_MNFA/m/91uDkgmR9Q0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One of our tests is for a simple inv_wishart sampler:

   transformed data {
     cov_matrix[3] S;
     S[1, 1] <- 2; S[1, 2] <- 0; S[1, 3] <- 0;
     S[2, 2] <- 1; S[2, 1] <- 0; S[2, 3] <- 0;
     S[3, 3] <- .5; S[3, 1] <- 0; S[3, 2] <- 0;
   }
   parameters {
     cov_matrix[3] W;
   }
   model {
     W ~ inv_wishart(5, S);
   }

The problem is that it's sometimes getting stuck and taking a very
long time for no effective samples.

Sometimes it runs really fast and provides almost reasonable estimates
(diagonals still not quite in the 95% intervals, but right on the
edge).

Anyone know more about this and want to take a look?

- Bob

